# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE ON www REDIRECTS — do not re-add a rule like:
#     https://www.example.com/*  https://example.com/:splat  301!
#
# It does not work. Cloudflare Pages only matches _redirects sources as PATHS.
# An absolute URL in the source position is silently ignored, so the rule looks
# correct, deploys without error, and never fires. Verified empirically: the
# rule was added here and to two sibling sites, all three deployed, none
# redirected. Sites that DO canonicalize correctly (coolbirdcounseling.com,
# safersoundsclub.com) have no such rule in _redirects at all — theirs is done
# at the Cloudflare zone level.
#
# The fix lives in the Cloudflare dashboard, not this file:
#   Zone -> Rules -> Redirect Rules -> Create rule
#     If  Hostname equals <the hostname to retire>
#     Then Dynamic redirect, 301, preserving path and query
#
# Alternative if it must live in the repo: a Pages Function at
# functions/_middleware.js can redirect on hostname. That turns on the Functions
# runtime for every request on this project, so the dashboard rule is preferable
# for a purely static site.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
